# ArtisanLoft Furniture — Project Context

## What this is
A furniture e-commerce app being rebuilt into a real, production-grade SaaS product.
Original version was scaffolded via Replit/Gemini and has known issues (see below).

## Stack
- Frontend: React (CRA) + Tailwind CSS, in /frontend — KEEP as-is structurally, only fix bugs
- Backend: Python FastAPI in /backend-fastapi
- ORM: SQLAlchemy + Alembic migrations
- DB: MySQL
- Auth: JWT (python-jose or PyJWT), passwords hashed with passlib[bcrypt]
- Payments: Razorpay Python SDK, sandbox/test mode
- Config: pydantic-settings + .env, never hardcode secrets or URLs

## Non-negotiable rules
- No hardcoded API URLs, secrets, or DB credentials in source — always env vars
- CORS origins must be a configurable list, not a single hardcoded origin
- All passwords must be hashed, never stored plaintext
- Every new endpoint needs a matching pytest test
- Match existing frontend API contract where possible: /api/products, /api/products/{id}
- Keep responses in the same JSON shape the frontend already expects

## Known bugs to fix during this rebuild
- Orders were previously not persisted at all — must actually write to DB
- Order history was hardcoded mock data — must fetch real orders per logged-in user
- Cart was React state only, wiped on refresh — persist to localStorage at minimum
- Auth was fully client-side/fake — must be real backend-verified JWT auth
- Footer has dead links (href="#") — wire real routes or remove
- Profile Settings buttons had no handlers
- Wishlist button wasn't connected to the Wishlist tab

## Style
- Keep the existing earthy/stone + orange accent Tailwind design language, don't redesign visually
